{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777803-how-to-turn-a-garou-ghost-into-an-ancestor-spirit","id":777803,"title":"How to turn a Garou Ghost into an Ancestor Spirit ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T09:58:32-08:00","id":777803,"title":"How to turn a Garou Ghost into an Ancestor Spirit ?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm running a white howler campaign and i will use Cororuc for the players to meet one of their ancestors.<br /> as it's said in Umbra W20 p 101, he was the last of his tribe and was denied the right to become an ancestor spirit.<br /> <br /> My idea is if the player succeed they could find this ghost turn it into an ancestor spirit and he could teach them the gifts related to the ghost of the original white howler tribe.<br /> It could also allow thew to start to open the Ancestor Background.<br /> <br /> <br /> So i have some question<br /> <br /> In what (in WW) is a Bashee different from a ghost (because for exemple fianna &amp; White Howler have gift offered by banshee) ?<br /> Does the player need to turn the ghost into a spirit to learn Gift ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T11:32:00-08:00","id":777838,"title":"","content":"hmmm, that is a tough one... I know, there is an Hengeyokai-rite, but that needs the body of the departed, and their cearn has to mourn and tell his tale before he can be taken...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T11:53:44-08:00","id":777843,"title":"","content":"Corocuc can't become an anscestor spirit because the White Howlers no longer have an Ancestral home, it has been corrupted by the BSD. I would resolve this by having an umbral quest at some point to create/discover a new home for them in the umbra. <br /> <br /> To your other question, A Banshee is just the Fianna term for a Ghost with specific Arcanoi if you are using WtO for cross over purposes. To simplify your life just treat ghost as a different kind of spirit, like how their are apparitions in the other realms. Gift can be learned from ghosts in WtA without making them the same as preumbra spirits, just not strange to them because ghosts typically don't know how to share their abilities the same way 'normal' spirits do. Typically I would say they need to learn the gift the hard way as they try to emulate their would be teacher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:21:36-08:00","id":778158,"title":"","content":"I don't see that a tribal homeland is relevant for an ancestor spirits. There aren't beed or auspice homelands, but homid ancestor spirits are often mentioned as teaching gifts.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think that a banshee is a wraith/ghost whatsoever. A banshee is a spirit from the part of the umbra garou normally travel to.<br /> <br /> I haven't read W20 Umbra but just read the Coruroc entry on the white wolf wiki. As a wraith with a wraith pack he basically can't become something else, except falling to oblivion or reaching transcendence. However, it might be possible, that a wraith can be subject to &quot;mallable spirit&quot; (rank 5 Thurge gift) and at a difficulty 10 can be turned gradually into a spirit of the middle umbra like an ancestor spirit.<br /> Also, one could try to backup his personality magically, then have him resurrected or reborn in some way and then put the old personality back in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T05:42:03-08:00","id":778266,"title":"","content":"If we follow the Umbra W20 a part of their Ancestral home is still pure. One hill only, but still better than nothing. I have some idea anyway about this already going on, but it could be another thing to go through before getting any ancestor spirits back.<br /> <br /> For the link between the realm and the ancestor it can be, and not.<br /> The Silent strider don't have access to their realm, and lost with that the access to their ancestors.<br /> On an other hand some tribes don't have access to the background Ancestor because they don't have a culture related with ancestor's cult's.<br /> <br /> As i know nothing about Wraith i think i'll use Ghost like a &quot;family&quot; type of spirit. As they said in UmbraW20, gift that target spirit don't work on ghost unless they specifically target their type. (Command spirits, things like this)<br /> <br /> <br /> So in the end, i can make an system a bit different to learn gift from ghost with no obligation to turn him back into an Ancestor Spirit.<br /> <br /> But the idea with the &quot;mallable spirit&quot; is good also, they would have to find a very good theurge, and then have the possibility to get access to a &quot;canon&quot; ancestor spirit if it succeed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:17:09-08:00","id":778284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777803-how-to-turn-a-garou-ghost-into-an-ancestor-spirit?p=778266#post778266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the link between the realm and the ancestor it can be, and not.<br /> The Silent strider don't have access to their realm, and lost with that the access to their ancestors.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were cursed and their homeland is hard to find, but some umbra travellers managed. Still, no ancestor spirits there... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777803-how-to-turn-a-garou-ghost-into-an-ancestor-spirit?p=778266#post778266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an other hand some tribes don't have access to the background Ancestor because they don't have a culture related with ancestor's cult's.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. The whole &quot;couldn't become ancestor spirit because homeland was corrupted&quot; in W20 Umbra seems to be not very thought through. One could argue the homeland can but doesn't have to be catalyst to create ancestor spirits - but I always hated the idea that ancestor spirits were garou ghosts. So, I'd just ignore the whole sentence and go with - the last white howler is a wraith and has a pack of other wraiths who were former BSD souls but have since been soulforged ... errr, I mean cleansed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}